<title>EGYPT: Egypt drugs firm profits up in 1995/6.</title>
<headline>Egypt drugs firm profits up in 1995/6.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis Pharmaceuticals and Chemical Industries made net after-tax of 19.786 million pounds in the financial year 1995/6, 54.7 percent up on 12.788 million in 1994/5, according to audited results available on Sunday.</p>
<p>The years end on June 30.</p>
<p>Turnover rose to 117.641 million pounds, 2.3 percent up on 115.033 million in the previous year, and profits before tax were 25.747 million, 26.8 percent up on 20.307 million.</p>
<p>The state privatised 40 percent of the company's 2.5 million shares earlier this month at 50.00 pounds each. The shares opened on the Egyptian stock exchange on Sunday at 61.00.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.4 pounds</p>
<p>-- Mona Eltahawy +2 02 578 3290/1</p>
